Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:24:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] packing/shader_split: read REDengine RDHS and FZLC shader
 caches (The Witcher 3)

The game keeps its precompiled NVN shaders in content/*/shadernx.cache
(an RDHS v3 container: u64 hash, u8 1, u32 raw, u32 stored, a zstd
frame records, one GLSLC output each) and staticshadernx.cache (FZLC
chunked zstd, then u64, u64, u32 length, GLSLC output records). The
generic scan saw none of the compressed records: the split wrote 539
shaders where the runtime asked for thousands of keys it did not have,
only a few draws landed each frame and the screen stayed black. The
split now writes 9,344; the keys seen missing at startup are covered.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#2694
Reason: The Witcher 3 keeps its precompiled NVN shaders in REDengine caches the split did not read
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#1318

